IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- HELPERS for every snap2 module: three-valued (Kleene) logic over MAYBE BOOLEAN.
-- JUST TRUE is "the text says yes", JUST FALSE is "the text says no", NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- Not a provision of the Act: the names begin with the label of the section they serve (s 2015) so that they cannot
-- collide with any other part's names. No source quotation is needed because nothing here is law.

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015 helper: both answers hold` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF b EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF a EQUALS JUST TRUE AND b EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015 helper: at least one answer holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF b EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF a EQUALS JUST FALSE AND b EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015 helper: the answer reversed` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (NOT x)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015 helper: every answer in the list holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) xs THEN JUST FALSE
        IF elem NOTHING xs THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015 helper: some answer in the list holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST TRUE) xs THEN JUST TRUE
        IF elem NOTHING xs THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- An integer count of whole months between two dates is not needed: periods are measured with `add months`.
-- The later of two dates (s 2015(d)(1)(C): "the later of").
GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2015 helper: the later of two dates` MEANS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

-- The earlier of two numbers (s 2015(d)(1)(B): "the lesser of").
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2015 helper: the lesser of two numbers` MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

-- The higher of two numbers (s 2015(d)(1)(A)(iii): "the higher of").
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2015 helper: the higher of two numbers` MEANS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b
